        "theory": "1.1.1 Place value\n\nWe can show rational number as whole number and decimal number in the place value table. Hamid bought a house in Rs 429716853. Show this value in place value chart.\n\nStandard Form:\n\n429,716,853\n\nPlace Value Form:\n\nNote it down\n\nEach digit has its value depending upon its position.\n\nPlace value tells us the position of\n\ndigits in a number.\n\nThere are 3 ones; 3 x 1 = 3\n\nThere are 8 hundreds; 8 x 100 = 800\n\nThere are 1 ten thousand; 1 x 10,000 = 10,000\n\nThere are 5 tens; 5 × 10 = 50\n\nThere are 6 thousands; 6 x 1000 = 6000\n\nThere are 7 hundred thousands; 7 x 100,000 = 700,000 There are 9 millions; 9 x 1,000,000 = 9,000,000\n\nThere are 2 ten millions; 2 x 10,000,000 = 20,000,000\n\nThere are 4 hundred millions; 4 x 100,000,000 = 400,000,000\n\nExpanded Form:\n\nIt shows a number as a sum of the values of all its digits. 429,716,853 = 400,000,000+ 20,000,000 + 9,000,000 + 700,000 + 10,000+ 6000 + 800 + 50 +3\n\nLets us find the place value of decimal number 532.678.\n\nStandard Form: 532.678\n\nQuick Check\n\nShow the number 85402314 in\n\nthe place value table.\n\nExpanded Form: It shows a number as a sum of the values of all its digits.\n\n532.678 = 500 +30 +2 +6 10+ 10+1000\n\n8 1000\n\nWe can also write it as: 532.678 = 500 + 30+2 +0.6+0.07+ 0.008\n\nPlace Value Form:\n\nEach digit has its value depending upon its position.\n\nThere are 8 thousandths;\n\n= 0.008\n\n1000\n\nThere are 7 hundredths; 100\n\n0.07\n\n(-); point\n\nThere are 6 tenths; =0.6\n\nThere are 2 ones; 2x1 = 2\n\nThere are 5 hundreds; 5 x 100 = 500\n\nThere are 3 tens; 3 x 10 = 30",
