        "title": "1.2 Rounding off Numbers",
        "theory": "1.2 Rounding off Numbers\n\nWe can round off numbers to get a rough idea or an estimate. An estimate might be a little more or less than the actual number. It is useful when we measure, tell the time or do sums.\n\nThe rules of rounding is as below:\n\nNote it down\n\nRounding off means to\n\nchange the value of a\n\nnumber to the one that is\n\neasier to work with.\n\nTo round off a number to a particular place, look at the digit to its right. If it is 5 or more, round up (to the greater 10, 100 or 1000). If it is 4 or less, round down (to the smaller 10, 100 or 1000).",
