        "theory": "1.6.1 Comparing and Ordering Whole numbers\n\nAmir has Rs 485,812 in his bank account and Faraz has Rs 485,697 in his bank account. Who has more money in his bank account?\n\nFirst compare the digits in the hundred thousands place. They are the same. Then compare the digits in the ten thousands place. They are the same. Now, we will compare the digits in the thousands place. They are also the same. So, we will compare the digits in the hundreds place.\n\n8 is greater than 6, i.e. 8> 6. So, 485,812 485,697.\n\nOrdering Whole numbers\n\nThe arrangement of numbers from smallest to greatest is called ascending order.\n\n64, 183; 64, 913;64,999 is in ascending order.\n\nNote it down\n\nWe use symbols that means less than or equal to and symbol z which means greater than or equal to.\n\nQuick Check\n\nThe correct symbol for. 23,897\n\n34,286. i) < ii) > iii) ≤\n\nThe arrangement of numbers from greatest to smallest is called descending order. 64,999;64, 913; 64, 183 is in descending order.\n\niv) 2\n\nTell the students to count the number of digits in each number and explain how to compare 4, 5 and 6- digit numbers using the place value chart.",
