        "solution": "To find the ratio of the new length of the ribbon to the original length, first find the new length of the ribbon.\nNew length of the ribbon = Original length of the ribbon - Length of Used ribbon\n= 72 cm-27 cm\n= 45 cm\nNow find the ratio.\nNew Length of the ribbon: Original length of the ribbon:\n575595\n45:\n5 8\nNote it down\nIf the ratio of the new quantity to the old one is in the form of an improper fraction, then the new quantity is greater than the old quantity.\nIf the ratio of the new quantity to an old quantity is in the form of a proper fraction, then the new amount will be smaller than the old quantity.\nSo, the length of the ribbon is decreased in the ratio 5: 8. In other words, the new length of\nthe ribbon is 5/8 times the original length of the ribbon.\nWe can also find the new quantity if the decrease or increase in the ratio is given."
