        "problem": "A worker works in a factory for 15 hours in a day. If he decreases the working hours in the ratio 4:5, what are his new working hours?\nOld working hours = 15\nRatio = 4:5\nDecreased hours =\nx 15 = 12 hours x\nSo, the new working hours after a decrease in the ratio 4:5, will be 12 hours\nQuick Check\nA company gives Rs 40,000 bonus to each of its employees annually.\nIf company increases that bonus in ratio 9:7, what is the new bonus that did each person get?",
