        "solution": "Suppose that the fourth proportional is x. Then we can write that as: 2:4::6:x.\nApplying cross product rule\nProduct of extremes = Product of means)\n2xx\n2x\n4 x 6\nI\n24 + 2\nTypes of Proportion\nThere are two types of proportion.\ni) Direct Proportion\nii) Inverse Proportion\ni) Direct Proportion\nIf with the increase in one quantity, the other quantity is increased and with the decrease in one quantity, the other quantity is decreased then these quantities are directly proportional each other. This relationship between quantities is called direct proportion.\nLet's consider a few examples.\n⚫\nNumber of articles and its cost is also directly proportional.\nNumber of items and their weights are also directly proportional. ⚫ Time available and work done is also directly proportional.\nA number and its multiple are directly proportional. As the number increases, its multiple also increases."
