        "problem": "A tailor stitches 5 dresses in 3 hours. How many dresses can he stitch in 12 hours?",
        "solution": "Here, time is directly proportional to the number of dresses he stitches.\nDresses\nTime\nThe same directional arrows indicate that as the number of dresses increases, the number of hours increases, so we have\n335/-----/3/23\nxx3 = 5 x 12\nxx3=60\nx = 60+3\nx=20\nHence, he stitches 20 dresses in 12 hours.\nii) Inverse Proportion\nIf with the increase in one quantity, the other quantity decrease and with the decrease of one quantity, the other quantity increase then these quantities inversely proportional to each other. This relationship between quantities is called inverse proportion.\nLet's consider a few examples.\nSpeed of a vehicle and the time to reach the destination are inversely proportional to\neach other.\nThe thermostat of an air conditioner is inversely proportional to the cooling of the said room. As the thermostat of an air conditioner decreases, the cooling of the said\nroom increases."
