        "solution": "Monthly income of Ali (gross salary) = Rs 60,000\nAnnual Income\n= Rs 60,000 × 12 = Rs 720,000\nAmount paid as Zakat\n= Rs 5500\nNet income\nRs 720,000 - Rs 5500 = 714500\nRebate\n= Rs 400000\nTaxable income\n= Rs 714500-Rs 400000 = Rs 314500\nIncome tax @ 5% = Rs 5% of Taxable income = 5% of Rs 314500\n* 100 = Rs 15725\nSo, he paid Rs 15725 as income tax.\nProperty Tax\nMath History\nThe tax which is paid on a property (house, shop, land, etc.) by its Abu-Al-Wafa (940-998 AD)\nowner is called property tax. In Pakistan property tax is a\nprovincial tax imposed on the citizens from the government.\nworked on arithmetic\ninvolving different kinds of problems on taxes as well\nProperty tax is based on the annual value of a property. The rates as problems of exchange\nof property tax can vary.\nLet's understand the concept of property tax by solving some"
