        "problem": "and valuation.\nFind the amount of the property tax paid by an owner of a house worth Rs 7,600,000 at the rate of 5%.",
        "solution": "Value of the house = Rs 7600000\nTax rate = 5%\nQuick Check\nProperty tax = 5% of Rs 7600000= 5% x Rs 7600000\n* Rs 7600000 = Rs 380000\nFind the property tax on a property of Rs 9,200,000 at the rate of 1.7%.\nExplain the student the term income tax and texable amount write different amounts on the board and ask them to tell the amount is taxable and how much amount have to be paid as tax on the given amount.\nGeneral Sales Tax (GST)\nA tax which is imposed by the government on the sale of goods or services bought by people using money is called general sales tax. General sales tax is decided by the government in percentage on the selling price of items. In Pakistan some basic items including wheat, rice, pulses, vegetables, meat, poultry etc. are exempted from general\nsales tax.\nLet's solve some examples related to GST for better understanding."
