        "solution": "Total Savings = Rs 1,56,000\nRate of Zakat = 2.5%\nAmount of Zakat =?\nAmount of Zakat = 2.5% of Rs 156000\n2.5 x 156000 = Rs 3900\nThus, Subhaan will pay Rs 3900 as Zakat.\nUshr\nUshr is the Zakat paid by Muslims (farmers) on their agricultural products. Ushr is charged at the rate of 10% on agricultural production if irrigated by natural water sources like springs, rivers, rainfall, etc. and 5% if irrigated by artificial means like tube wells, wells, canals, etc. Example:\nTotal worth of the crop = Rs 366400\nRate of Ushr\n= 10%\nAmount of Ushr\n= ?\nAmount of Ushr\n10% of Rs 366400\nx 366400 = Rs 36640\nLuck\nQuick Check\nFind the total amount of the Zakat on the yearly savings of Rs 95.900.\nNote it down\nUshr means one-tenth.\nNote it down\nProphet Muhammad()said: Al-Islam is raised on five (pillars), testifying (the fact) that there is no God but Allah, that Muhammad is His bondsman and messenger, and the establishment of prayers, payment of Zakat Pilgrimage to the House (Kaabah) and the fact of Ramadan.\n(Sahih Muslim: 16)\nThus, amount of Ushr is Rs 36,640."
