        "theory": "6.3.1 Operations on Sets\n\nWe have learnt how to carry out the four basic arithmetic operations on whole numbers, fractions and decimals. Now we will learn about some special operations on sets. The operations are performed when the sets are expressed in tabular form.\n\nLet's learn about the following basic operations on sets.\n\n1. Union of sets\n\nThe union of two or more sets is a set which consists of all the elements of both sets. The operation is done by combining the elements of two or more sets into a single set. In union of sets,\n\nNote it down\n\nUnion of two given sets is the smallest set which contains all the elements of both sets.\n\nwe do not write an element more than once. The symbol for denoting union of sets is . We write the union of two sets A and B as AUB and read it as \"A union B\".",
