        "solution": "Here, the elements 3 and 5 are common in both sets Uand V. So, UV = (3, 5). Example 2:\nIf G= (0, 1, 2, 3), H = (2, 3, 4) and I = {3, 5, 6, 7), then find GnHl.\nFirst find GOH.\nIf G= (0, 1, 2, 3}, H = {2, 3, 4}\nGH = {2, 3}\nNate it down\nIntersection of two given sets is the smallest set which contains all the\nelements that are common to both sets.\nWrite two or three sets on the board. Call students randomly and ask them to find their union. Ask the remaining students to check if he/she has done it correctly.\nLet's denote this set GoH as X.\nSo, X = {2, 3)\nNow find Xol.\nX = (2, 3) and I = (3, 5, 6, 7)\nXnl = (3)\nSo, GnHol = Xnl = (3).\n3. Difference of two sets\nLet's consider two sets A and B. The difference A - B is a set of all those elements of set A which are not the elements of set B. It is denoted by A-B or A\\B."
