        "title": "7.8 Factorization of Algebraic Expression",
        "theory": "7.8 Factorization of Algebraic Expression\n\nAs we know that factorization of a number means to break it into numbers that can be multiplied together to get the original number.\n\nFor example; 8 = 2 x 4, so factors of 8 are 2 and 4.\n\n2 x 4 = 8\n\nFactors Product\n\nNote it down\n\nFactorization of an algebraic expression is the process of finding the factors of it. It is the reverse process of expansion.\n\nSimilarly, in algebraic expressions the product of y and y+a is y+ay. Here, y and y+a are the factors of y+ay. Algebraic expression can be factorised by common factors, algebraic identities and making groups.",
