            "question": "Factorize by middle-term breaking.\na) 2x²+5x+2\nb) x²−9x+18\nc) x²+3x−4=0\nd) x²−12x+35\ne) x²+5x+4\nf) 9x²+6x+1\ng) 2x²+7x+3",
            "solution": "Split the middle term into factors of the constant term whose sum is the x coefficient.\na) 2x²+4x+x+2=(2x+1)(x+2).\nb) x²−3x−6x+18=(x−3)(x−6).\nc) x²+4x−x−4=(x−1)(x+4); therefore x=1 or x=−4.\nd) x²−5x−7x+35=(x−5)(x−7).\ne) x²+x+4x+4=(x+1)(x+4).\nf) (3x+1)².\ng) 2x²+6x+x+3=(2x+1)(x+3)."
