        "id": "we-7-1",
        "title": "Examples",
        "problem": "A grdener is planting flower plants in park. First day he planted 100 flowers, next day he planted 89 flowers, 3rd day 78 flowers, and so on. If he continues this pattern, how many flowers will he plant on 4th, 5th and 6th day respectively?\nLet's arrange the number of flowers in sequence. 100, 89, 78,\nFirstly, work out the difference in the terms. This pattern is going down by 11 each time, so we will subtract 11 from the last term to find the next term in the pattern. 100, 89, 78, 67, 56, 45.\nSo, he will plant 67, 56 and 45 flowers on 4th, 5th and 6th day respecyiely.\nPosition to terms rule\nPosition to terms rule helps us to find out what number\nis in a pattern if its position in the pattern is given. Example 1:\nNote it down\nTo work out the term-to-term rule, give the starting number of the sequence and then describe the pattern of the numbers. Once the first term and term to term rule are known, all the terms in the pattern can be found.\nFind the position to term rule to find 20th term of the pattern: 10, 11, 12, 13, 14,",
        "solution": "First, write the terms and their positions of this pattern in a table.\nPosition\nTerm\nNow find the rule for position to terms\nPosition\nTerm\nRule\n1+9\n2+9\n3+9\n4+9\n5+9\n6+9\nWe see that each term is obtained by adding 9 to the position of the term. Now, to find the 20\" term of this pattern, we will add 9 to 20.\nSo, the 20\" Term is: 20 + 9 = 29.\nSimilarly, if we denote any general term as n, then the position to term rule is here is n + 9. The nth term\nThe nth term of a sequence is the general term that can help us find any term of the sequence. We can find any term by putting the value in the nth term.\nLets consider the nth term: 2n +1.\nBy putting n=1, we get the 1\" term.\n1\" term of this sequence = 2(1)+1=2+1=3\nPut n=2, we get 2 term.\n2\" term of this sequence = 2(2)+1=4+1=5\nTo find any term, say 9, Put n=9, we get 9 term.\nSo, 9o term of this sequence = 2(9)+1=18+1=19\nLet's observe the examples:"
