        "title": "Example 1",
        "problem": "Factorize x2-5x + 4 by middle term breaking method.",
        "solution": "In order to factorize - 5x+4, we have to find two numbers such that their sum is -5 and their product is (+1)x(+4) = +4\nClearly, (-4)+(-1)=-5 and (-4) x (-1) = +4\nWe now split the middle term 5x of x-5x+4 as-4x-x.\nx2-5x+4= x2-4x-x+4\n= x(x-4)-1(x-4)\n= (x − 1)(x-4)\nSo, the factors of x-5x+4 are (x-1) and (x-4)."
