        "solution": "In order to factorize 3x-10x-8, we have to find two numbers such that their sum is -10\nand their product is (+3) (-8)=-24\nClearly, -12 + 2 = -10 and -12 x 2 = -24\nWe now split the middle term 10x of 3x2-10x-8 as -12x + 2x.\n3r2-10x-8=3x-12x+2x-8\n3x(x-4)+2(x-4)=(3x-2)(x-4)\nSo, the factors of 3x2-10x-8 are (3x-2) and (x-4)"
