        "id": "8.1",
        "title": "8.1 Solving Linear Equations",
        "theory": "8.1 Solving Linear Equations\n\nA linear equation in one variable is an open sentence. The process to find the value of the involved variable which makes the linear equation\n\nMath History\n\nMuhmmad Ibn Musa Al-Khwarizmi (780-850 AD), A Muslim mathematician, in his book entitled \"Kitab Al-Jabr wa'l-Muqabala gives the systematic solution of linear equations.\n\ntrue is known as its solution. The value of the variable which satisfies the equation is known as the root or solution of the equation. When solving an equation, we actually look for the value of the variable that satisfies the equation and makes it true. During this we try to separate the variable alone on one side of the equation and gather the remaining terms/constants/coefficients on the other side. This process of separating the variable on one side of the equation is called \"isolation of variable\". Let's recall some properties of equality.",
