        "text": "8.2 Real Life Problems:\n\nThe concept of linear equations helps us in various situations of our daily life. We often need to find an unknown quantity when there is enough information about other factors and the condition of factors are given. In order to solve real-life problems related to linear equations, we need to translate them into mathematical equations. Then solve them by using the techniques for solving linear equations and we find an unknown quantity easily. Let's consider the following examples.",
