            "solution": "Apply the same operation to both sides; substitute each result to verify.\na) 8x=−10.5, x=−21/16. Check: −10.5+0.5=−10.\nb) x=−1/3. Check: −99(−1/3)=33.\nc) −5x=−31/4, x=31/20.\nd) (8+16/5)x=10; (56/5)x=10, x=25/28.\ne) 6=16x, x=3/8.\nf) −12=8x+4, x=−2.\ng) 2.4=6.16x, x=30/77.\nh) 18x=128, x=64/9.\ni) Since 0.6/0.5=1.2, 0.3x−0.6=6x−4.8; x=14/19 (and 5x−4≠0).\nj) 10x=−6, x=−3/5.\nk) Cross multiply: 6(5x−0.3)=5(7x−2.1); x=87/50."
