        "theory": "Student Learning Outcomes\n\nAfter completing this unit, students will be able to: .Convert different units of distance.\n\n. Convert 12-hour clock to 24-hour clock and vice versa.\n\nConvert between different units of time and speed.\n\n. Calculate arrival time, departure time and journey time in a given situation (on the previous day and the\n\nnext day).\n\n. Solve real world word problems involving distance, time and average speed.\n\n. Differentiate between uniform and average speeds.\n\nரடை\n\nA plane took off from city A at 10:20 a.m. and reached its destination at 12:40 p.m. How much time did it take to reach from city A to city B?\n\nIntroduction/\n\nversa.\n\nWe have learned how to convert larger units to smaller units of time and vice In this unit we will learn about different units of distance, time and speed. We will learn about arrival time, departure time and journey time and also differentiate between uniform and average speed.",
