        "title": "10.1 Conversion of Unit of Distance",
        "theory": "10.1 Conversion of Unit of Distance\n\nThe following is the relationship between units of measure of distance.\n\n1 kilometre (km)\n\n1 metre (m)\n\n1 centimetre (cm)\n\n= 1000 metres (m)\n\n= 100 centimetres (cm)\n\n= 10 millimetres (mm)\n\nConversion of Kilometres to Metres\n\na) To convert kilometres to metres, we multiply the number of kilometres by 1000. Example 1:\n\nConvert 5 km to m.\n\nSolution:\n\n5 km = 5 x 1000 m = 5000 m\n\nb) To convert kilometres and metres to metres only, we multiply the number of\n\nkilometres by 1000 and add metres to it.",
