        "theory": "10.1.1 Conversion of Metres to Kilometres\n\na) To convert metres to kilometres, we divide the number of metres by 1000. Example 1:\n\nConvert 7000 m to km.\n\nSolution:\n\n7000 m = (7000 + 1000) km = 7 km\n\nANG\n\nRecall a few basic concepts about time, distance and their units that they have learned in previous grades. Then ask some concept related question or take a short quiz about the concepts. This will\n\nhelp the student recall their prior learning.\n\nTo convert metres to kilometres and metres, we divide the number of metres by 1000. The quotient will be the kilometres and the remainder will be the metres.",
