        "theory": "A polygon is a closed plane figure made from three or more straight line segments called sides. Triangles and quadrilaterals are polygons. In this unit the sides meet only at their endpoints and do not cross each other.\n\nA closed figure can be traced from a starting point back to the same point without a break. Being closed alone does not make a figure a polygon: its boundary must also consist of straight segments. The curved outline in the source note illustrates closure, not a polygon.",
