            "qNo": "1",
            "question": "Draw and describe properties of: a) square b) rectangle c) parallelogram d) rhombus e) trapezium f) kite. Include parallel/equal sides, equal/right angles and symmetry.",
            "solution": "a) Square: 4 equal sides, 4 right angles, two pairs of parallel opposite sides, 4 symmetry axes (two medians and two diagonals). The book text says 6 axes, but that is incorrect.\nb) Rectangle: opposite sides equal and parallel, 4 right angles, 2 symmetry axes.\nc) Parallelogram: opposite sides equal and parallel; opposite angles equal; adjacent angles sum to 180°; generally no symmetry axis.\nd) Rhombus: 4 equal sides, opposite sides parallel, opposite angles equal, adjacent angles supplementary; 2 diagonal symmetry axes.\ne) Trapezium: one pair of opposite sides parallel; same-side interior angles on each leg sum to 180°. Isosceles trapezium has one symmetry axis.\nf) Kite: two pairs of adjacent equal sides; one pair of opposite angles equal; one symmetry axis.",
