        "problem": "Find each exterior angle of a regular octagon. Explain why one exterior angle at each vertex of a convex polygon totals 360°.",
        "solution": "At every vertex, the interior angle and its adjacent exterior angle make a straight angle of \\(180^\\circ\\). For n vertices their total is \\(180^\\circ n\\). Subtract the interior-angle sum: \\(180^\\circ n-180^\\circ(n-2)=360^\\circ\\). In a regular octagon the eight exterior angles are equal, so each is \\(360^\\circ/8=45^\\circ\\). Its interior angle is \\(180^\\circ-45^\\circ=135^\\circ\\). Check: \\(8\\times45^\\circ=360^\\circ\\). For concave polygons the full-turn result uses signed turning angles; do not add unsigned reflex-vertex turns as if every vertex were convex."
