        "theory": "A transformation changes a figure's position, orientation or size according to a rule. This unit studies reflection, rotation and translation. These three preserve lengths and angles, so the image has the same size and shape as the original.\n\nThe original figure is the pre-image; the transformed figure is its image. A reflection flips a figure in a mirror line, a rotation turns it about a centre, and a translation slides every point by the same movement.",
