            "qNo": "2",
            "question": "Decide whether each dotted line is a line of symmetry; then identify which figures have a line of symmetry.",
            "solution": "For the dotted lines actually shown: (a) No—the vertical line does not reflect B onto itself. (b) No—the vertical line does not reflect N onto itself. (c) Yes—the horizontal line reflects the drawn E onto itself. (d) Yes—the horizontal line bisects the narrow rectangular I-shaped figure into matching halves. (e) No—the vertical line fails for the offset step shape. (f) Yes—the vertical line passes through the centre of the oval. Therefore c,d,f have symmetry about their marked lines. The separate question 'Which figures have lines of symmetry?' also includes B (a), whose drawn matching lobes give a horizontal line, even though its displayed vertical line is wrong. N and the offset step do not have reflection symmetry in the pictured forms."
