            "question": "Encircle the correct option (pp.236–237).\n(a) A line of symmetry divides the symmetric shape into: (i) Quarters (ii) Halves (iii) Thirds (iv) Fourths.\n(b) If a figure looks exactly the same at least twice during a full rotation, it has: (i) Translation symmetry (ii) Reflective symmetry (iii) Rotational symmetry (iv) Line symmetry.\n(c) Turning a shape around a fixed centre of rotation is: (i) Reflection (ii) Translation (iii) Rotation (iv) Dilation.\n(d) Moving or shifting an object from one place to another is: (i) Reflection (ii) Translation (iii) Rotation (iv) Dilation.\n(e) Translating an object does not affect its: (i) Position (ii) Location (iii) Placement (iv) Size.\n(f)2 units left and1 unit down is: (i)(x,y)→(x+2,y−1) (ii)(x,y)→(x−2,y+1) (iii)(x,y)→(x+2,y+1) (iv)(x,y)→(x−2,y−1).\n(g) A90° counterclockwise or270° clockwise rotation about the origin will: (i) Change the sign of x and switch x,y (ii) Change the sign of x only (iii) Change the sign of y only (iv) Change the sign of y and switch x,y.\n(h)(x,y)→(x−4,y+6) means: (i) Add4 to x and6 to y (ii) Subtract4 from y and add6 to x (iii) Add4 to x and6 to y (iv) Subtract4 from x and add6 to y. Options(i) and(iii) are repeated in the source.",
