        "problem": "Explain the symmetry lines shown for the semicircle, isosceles trapezium, right-pointing arrow and sideways kite.",
        "solution": "(a) The semicircle has one vertical symmetry line through its centre and the midpoint of its diameter. Its left and right halves coincide. A horizontal line is not a symmetry line, because it would reflect the curved half below the diameter. (b) The isosceles trapezium has a vertical line through the midpoints of its parallel bases: its left and right halves match. (c) The arrow has a horizontal line through its centre: its top and bottom halves match. (d) The sideways kite has a horizontal line through the two vertices where equal-side pairs meet. In each case, reflecting every point across the marked line gives the same complete outline.",
