        "theory": "Organizing data in a frequency distribution helps us see patterns and trends. Sometimes we need one representative value to describe the dataset. Such a value is called an average or a measure of central tendency.\n\nThis section introduces three measures: arithmetic mean, median and mode. They describe different aspects of the data, so the choice depends on what we want to find out.",
