          "Sara's experiment: choose a number at random from {3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 10}. (a) Even numbers are {4, 6, 8, 10}, so \\(P(\\text{even})=\\frac46=\\frac23\\). The complement is {3, 7}, giving \\(P(\\text{not even})=1-\\frac23=\\frac13\\).",
          "(b) Factors of 12 present in the sample space are {3, 4, 6}. Therefore \\(P(\\text{factor of 12})=\\frac36=\\frac12\\). The other numbers {7, 8, 10} form the complement, so \\(P(\\text{not a factor of 12})=1-\\frac12=\\frac12\\). The printed solution mistakenly refers to an even number in this factor calculation; the event here is being a factor of 12."
